WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.167
-We're back with Colin Jost.

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:05.067
All jokes aside,
this is a really funny podcast

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:07.334
you do with Wanda Sykes,
and it's getting great reviews.

00:00:07.334 --> 00:00:11.033
-Um, yes, I was very --
Anything that gets good reviews

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:13.100
that I'm involved in,
I'm surprised.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.501
That's just my way
of thinking.

00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:18.267
But people were
very excited about it.

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:21.033
Our friend Claire Friedman
wrote it and she's fantastic.

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:23.300
I was very excited
to do it with Wanda.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.801
Wanda is in it.
Heidi Gardner is in it.

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:27.767
Cecily Strong, Neil Patrick
Harris, it's a great cast.

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:29.868
-You got Parnell.
-Parnell. That's right.

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:33.801
I'm definitely the worst one
by a large margin.

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:36.701
-That's not true.
But are you a little, um...

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:39.000
-I get suspicious.
-About the reviews?

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.567
-The reviews.
Do you ever see reviews

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:41.968
that they're so good
that you're like,

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:44.167
"This wasn't a human
that wrote this"?

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:45.501
-Like, here's one. "Hilarious.

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:47.167
The character development
is so specific

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:48.534
and the actors
are perfectly cast.

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:50.200
I've laughed out loud
so many times

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.534
and can picture all of it."

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:54.267
Five, five, five.

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.868
-Five, five, five. Hilarious.
Also, I think also this is

00:00:56.868 --> 00:01:00.434
a little bit of a brag
about their own imagination.

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:02.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.234 --> 00:01:04.634
You know? They're like,
"I can picture all of it.

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:06.334
You might not be able to."
-Yeah.

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:08.634
You do feel like if there was
a second -- a fourth row

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:09.901
that said, like,
"my imagination,"

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.300
there'd be five stars there.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.901
-It would be six.
"I imagine another star."

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:16.167
-Yeah. "Funniest thing
I've heard in a while.

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:17.400
Claire Friedman is a genius.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.133
Colin Jost and Wanda Sykes
are incredible together.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.567
Everything about
this is perfect.

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.267
It's like listening to
an amazing episode of '30 Rock.'

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.834
Cannot recommend enough"
is another one, all five.

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:26.901
-Genius. Claire Friedman,
a friend of mine.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:29.400
Would I say genius? Um...

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.501
"Colin Jost and Wanda Sykes
are incredible.

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:35.133
Enjoying it is perfect.

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:37.400
It's like listening
to an amazing episode," right.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.634
And then I like that one person
found it helpful.

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:41.501
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.167
-And I will admit, that was me.

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:45.634
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:47.367
-I was like,
"This is very helpful for me."

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:49.434
-This is the -- This again,

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:52.133
I would say with the words
still is positive.

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:53.634
-Yes. "Hilarious.

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:56.834
I listened to this
in one day at work."

00:01:56.834 --> 00:02:00.067
Meanwhile, like, what's
the employer thinking right now?

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:03.434
That's like eight hours of work
that they spent listening to it

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:05.267
"and was literally
laughing out loud."

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.567
Overall, five stars
performance, five stars.

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:10.567
Story, two stars.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:13.200
So...
-Feels weird to be so positive

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.501
and then be like, "Story stunk."

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:17.100
-Yeah, story. But anyway,
really, check out the story.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:21.734
I know you're like, "I bet
the story is going to be good."

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:23.167
It will be. Don't listen to...

00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:24.534
-I mean,
when you average it out,

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:26.667
it's still like, you know, with
those other two fives,

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:27.701
still comes out to like a four.

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:30.334
-Probably like high threes.
-Yeah.

00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:32.634
-I'm no math guy.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:34.901
-We didn't get into this
because we're math guys.

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:36.100
-Is it called math guy?

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.601
-That was right before,
on that red carpet,

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:40.133
someone asked you
what's 12 divided by 3?

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:47.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:49.000
Your mom had a birthday
or has one coming up?

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.367
-My mom's birthday
is on Sunday. I'm very excited.

00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:54.334
-Very big fan of your mom.

00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:56.400
-Doctor Kerry Kelly.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.834
She was in the fire department
for a long time.

00:02:57.834 --> 00:02:59.968
She's turning 21,
which is pretty exciting.

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:02.267
-But how --
You did not know her age.

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:03.534
-All growing up,

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:06.801
she would tell my brother
and I that she --

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:08.534
Every birthday, we would
be like, "How old are you?"

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:10.834
We don't ask now because
we don't want to know the truth.

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:13.033
But when we were young,
we would ask like,

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:14.767
"How old are you turning?"
And she would always say,

00:03:14.767 --> 00:03:16.133
21 when we were kids.

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:17.868
-Yeah.
-She was like, "I'm 21."

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:21.267
And you know
I'm a fairly gullible person.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.167
-Yeah.
-If you've ever seen me

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:27.033
on "Weekend Update" and perhaps
I've gotten tricked at times,

00:03:27.033 --> 00:03:28.701
you may see me and say,

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:31.200
"That is -- I can't believe
how gullible this man is."

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.434
-Yep.
-So as a kid I was also that.

00:03:33.434 --> 00:03:35.167
And so when she would
tell me and my brother

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.767
she was turning 21 every year,

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:42.767
I believed it for a very long
time, until I was like 12.

00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:45.467
And one of my friends asked
how old my mom was

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:47.501
and I said, "She's turning 21."

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:50.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:52.734
And they were like,
"Oh, no, what happened?"

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:55.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.734
"Is she okay?
Is everything okay?"

00:03:57.734 --> 00:04:00.767
And I was like, "Yeah, it's
fine. She's 21, I'm 12."

00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:02.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:04.367
And then they told their parents

00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:06.868
and then my mom had to be like,
"I'm 45, you idiot."

00:04:06.868 --> 00:04:08.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.501 --> 00:04:10.868
-You brought a photo of your son
Cosmo last time you were here.

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:12.234
-Yeah, he just turned --

00:04:12.234 --> 00:04:14.033
He's two in a little bit,
a couple months.

00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:16.667
-Gotcha.
-And he's a cute kid.

00:04:16.667 --> 00:04:18.367
He's like -- He's doing
a lot of stuff.

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:20.133
He's like, very active.

00:04:20.133 --> 00:04:21.934
-Do you mind if we show a pic?
-No, no, no.

00:04:21.934 --> 00:04:23.901
That's okay. Yeah.
Please go ahead.

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:27.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:29.834
I feel like he has
his dad's sense of fashion.

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:32.501
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:34.467
-Thanks.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:37.634
Thanks for taking the time
to print that out to show that.

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:39.434
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.434 --> 00:04:42.367
-I was like,
"I know what'll be funny."

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:45.100
-We are gonna --
When a guest insists on

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.868
making an art card
and it goes that bad,

00:04:46.868 --> 00:04:48.033
we do make them pay for it.

00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:52.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:53.667
It's not much.

00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:55.634
-Yeah.
-It's not much, but we just...

00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:57.601
-I was like, "I got it."

00:04:57.601 --> 00:04:59.501
-I want to say --
I want to mention one member

00:04:59.501 --> 00:05:01.601
of your family
who recently passed.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:04.100
And I say this with all
sincerity, your grandmother.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:06.367
-Yes.
-Who I adored.

00:05:06.367 --> 00:05:08.167
And I remember the last time
I was lucky enough

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:10.200
to get to talk to her
was at your wedding.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.300
And it was so exciting
that she was there.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:14.968
She passed away.
Tell everybody how old.

00:05:14.968 --> 00:05:17.901
-My grandma just passed away.
She was 106 years old.

00:05:17.901 --> 00:05:19.534
[ Audience gasps ]
Yes.

00:05:19.534 --> 00:05:21.767
So it's not even --
No sympathy at that point.

00:05:21.767 --> 00:05:22.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:24.300
You tell people like,
"Oh, my grandma died,"

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.467
and they're like,
"Oh, my God, I'm so sorry.

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:27.334
How old was she?"
And you're like, "106."

00:05:27.334 --> 00:05:28.701
And they're like,
"Oh, so kind of late."

00:05:28.701 --> 00:05:32.434
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:34.767
She was turning -- She was 106.

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:37.234
And she survived COVID.
Like, she got through COVID.

00:05:37.234 --> 00:05:39.634
And so I remember calling her
when COVID started and I

00:05:39.634 --> 00:05:42.234
was like, "Grandma, are you
okay? Is everything okay?

00:05:42.234 --> 00:05:45.734
And I swear to God, she was
like, "First the Spanish flu."

00:05:45.734 --> 00:05:50.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.868 --> 00:05:52.968
"Now this."

00:05:52.968 --> 00:05:56.567
And I was like,
"How old are you?!"

00:05:56.567 --> 00:05:59.000
It's true.
It's literally the same years

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.868
as if it had been like, "First
the Titanic, now the submarine."

00:06:02.868 --> 00:06:05.067
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:06.334
-May she rest in peace.

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:08.200
She lived a long life.
We were lucky to have her.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.000
-We were very lucky.
-I was very lucky to know her.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.734
Thanks for being here, buddy.
It is just the best.

00:06:11.734 --> 00:06:13.767
Have a great show.

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:15.467
-Thanks for having me.
-That's Colin Jost, everybody.

00:06:15.467 --> 00:06:18.334
"Trust Fall" is on Audible now.
Audible.

